  The katana can be used two handed, and is in modern kendo schools,
however, it is not necessarily such.  One might think of it as a 
hand-and-a-half.
  I don't know about yours, but any of my kendo sensei would make
you do 500 tsuburi for saying that the katana is "designed for 
hacking things apart". 
  The wakizashi is really too long for seppuku, except in dire
emergency; rather, the tanto was used (a more dagger-like weapon).

